WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.950
The final trailer for the upcoming third season
of Stranger Things drops plenty of hints about

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.170
the characters' journeys.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.570
We also get some big clues about the villains
of the season, as well as a few obligatory

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.570
'80s Easter eggs.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.560
Let's take a look at the small details you
may have missed.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.160
The third season of Stranger Things will be
the first that doesn't take place during Halloween.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.910
Netflix revealed that season 3 would be dropping
on Independence Day 2019 with a special date

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.800
announcement, and the 4th of July holiday
will also be the setting of the show this

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.800
year.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.710
The final season 3 trailer opens with a wide
shot of a 4th of July fun fair sponsored by

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.710
Mayor Kline.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.800
A new character for season 3, Larry Kline
is portrayed by Cary Elwes, star of '80s classic

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.960
The Princess Bride.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.000
"But in the meantime, rest well and dream
of large women."

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.480
Promotional materials for the show describe
Kline as "handsome, slick and sleazy… your

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.100
classic '80s politician."

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.840
It looks like the mayor will be a secondary
villain of sorts, but could his arc tie in

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.570
to a previously unexplored plot?

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:02.789
We're going back to Hawkins in the summer
of 1985, at the height of the Cold War.

00:01:02.789 --> 00:01:06.910
Theory crafters are predicting that the Duffers
will return to the Russian spy subplot planted

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:11.010
by journalist-turned-private investigator
Murray Bauman in season 2.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.210
"Russian spies!

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.120
Are the Russian spies in cahoots with the
aliens?

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.640
Or how do they fit in here?"

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.960
"It doesn't make sense.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.130
I closed the gate."

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:26.270
With that line, Eleven is obviously referring
to the moment she used her psychokinetic powers

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.970
to seal the portal to the Upside Down at the
end of season 2, seemingly saving Hawkins

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.780
from the monstrous creatures that dwell on
the other side.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.040
It didn't take a genius to figure out that
the Upside Down would feature in the coming

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.340
third season, however, and the final trailer
confirms that this will indeed be the case.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.450
We see Eleven in her sense-depriving blindfold
early on in the trailer, surrounded by her

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.650
concerned friends.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.780
Her trademark nosebleed tells us that she's
using her special abilities, and the following

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.460
shot shows that she's in the hellscape that
is the Upside Down, standing in front of a

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.990
large steelworks warehouse.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.520
This warehouse appears to be the hideout of
the evil that will be unleashed this coming

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.520
season.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.300
We see a swarm of rats converging on the place,
and a dark smoke-like entity whirling its

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.920
way through the empty corridors.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.200
But is this entity a new foe, or one the gang
has faced before?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.760
Inside the Brimborn warehouse there's a brief
but unmistakable shot of the Mind Flayer,

00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:16.739
the creature that took control of Will Byers
in season 2.

00:02:16.739 --> 00:02:20.450
The young heroes of Hawkins thought they'd
locked the Mind Flayer in the Upside Down,

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.000
but as Byers points out, they don't know that
for sure.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.999
"What if we locked him out here with us?"

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:29.069
Byers is clearly still connected to the Mind
Flayer in some way, and he drops a huge clue

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:33.590
about the malevolent entity's intentions for
season 3 in the last trailer, saying that

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.159
it'll be looking for a new host.

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:39.319
The face of Billy Hargrove appears onscreen
as Byers utters the words, heavily implying

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.200
that the season 2 bully will become an even
bigger threat to the kids this time out.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.549
There's an ominous voiceover in the trailer
that has everybody scratching their heads.

00:02:47.549 --> 00:02:51.510
It begins right at the start of the trailer,
playing over some lingering shots of our tween

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.510
heroes.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.659
"You let us in."

00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:57.470
The same voice can be heard later in the trailer:

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:02.590
"We are going to end you, we are going to
end your friends."

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.459
The owner of the voice is never identified,
and there are a lot of theories, but listen

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:10.620
closely, and voice sounds an awful lot like
Jake Busey, a new addition to the Stranger

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.650
Things cast.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.659
He's playing a character called Bruce, a reporter
from The Hawkins Post who has, quote, "questionable

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:18.049
morals and a sick sense of humor."

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:19.769
Is he going to be an important villain?

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:23.760
Well put it this way: it's probably no coincidence
that Busey's character shares a name with

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.590
the shark from Steven Spielberg's Jaws.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:29.349
"Bruce got his name because my lawyer's name,
I named the shark after my lawyer.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.040
He's still my lawyer by the way."

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.879
We got our first good look at season 3 newbie
Maya Hawke in the Starcourt mall teaser that

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:38.170
Netflix dropped in July 2018.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:42.489
Hawke plays a character named Robin, a co-worker
of Steve Harrington at the sparkly new mall's

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:44.269
Scoops Ahoy ice cream parlor.

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:48.560
The first season 3 trailer showcased Robin
in this capacity, but now we know for sure

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.689
that she's going to be doing way more than
just scooping ice cream − there's a shot

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:55.760
of her peering through a glass door at something
that's probably not from this dimension.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.880
Another bewildering moment in the trailer
is when Steve and Dustin unearth a canister

00:03:59.889 --> 00:04:03.810
filled with something peculiar, and judging
by what Harrington is wearing at the time,

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.849
he's in the middle of a shift at Scoops Ahoy.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:09.730
It's one of the standout shots from the final
trailer, and it seems to indicate that something

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.140
is going on in the bowels of the Starcourt
mall.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.879
The next two shots feature people in hazmat
suits gathered around what appears to be some

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:17.630
kind of particle collider.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.500
The machine fires up and shoots a white beam
of energy, which could well be the cause of

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.880
the blackout at the end of the trailer.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.480
But who is experimenting under the mall?

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.880
"It's alive"

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.470
The Hawkins National Laboratory was shut down
after it was linked to the death of season

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:37.350
1 fan favorite Barbara Holland, though there
are bound to be plenty of other interested

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.120
parties when it comes to unlocking the secrets
of the Upside Down.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.960
There's lots of quick editing in the final
season 3 trailer, but if you watch it back

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.790
a couple of times you'll notice that a few
different teams seem to have formed by the

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.790
end.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.500
Eleven, Mike, and Max cower together behind
a counter, while Will, Jonathan, Nancy, and

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.540
Lucas take cover behind a battered car.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.850
Steve, Dustin, Robin, and Erica appear to
escape the mall.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:02.130
Lastly, there are the adults: Hopper, Joyce
and Murray.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.100
Joyce Byers had a thing with Sean Astin's
Bob Newby in season 2, but the Radio Shack

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.360
manager was killed helping the gang escape.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.880
Bob wasn't unpopular, but most Stranger Things
fans have been shipping a Joyce-Hopper relationship

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.370
since the early days of the show.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.790
A blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment in the final
trailer all but confirms that they'll make

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.190
the leap in season 3.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.280
The shot is a close-up of two unidentified
people holding hands.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.590
Pause it, and you'll notice that the shirts
they're wearing match the ones worn by Joyce

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.410
and Hopper earlier in the trailer.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.560
David Harbour is aware of how much people
want this, and he gets it.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.780
"The fans, they call it like 'Jopper,' or
something.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:43.190
They all ship this relationship with Hopper
and Joyce and I do too, because I feel like

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.200
they're two really lonely, lost people."

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.120
Stranger Things just wouldn't be Stranger
Things without all the '80s Easter eggs, and

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.880
there are going to be plenty of those in the
upcoming third season.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.890
Ross Duffer kept his cards close when IndieWire
asked him which films he and his brother would

00:05:55.890 --> 00:06:00.850
be referencing this time out, but the final
season 3 trailer contains a few subtle clues.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.300
Lucas, for example, wears an outfit reminiscent
of The Karate Kid.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.540
One of the most blatant nods to an iconic
movie comes when Max, Eleven and Mike take

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.260
cover behind a counter in the mall.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:14.370
The shot is super similar to the kitchen scene
from Jurassic Park, which is of course an

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.810
early '90s movie, but seeing as it's directed
by Steven Spielberg, it's fair game.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.640
The Duffer brothers have made no secret of
the fact that they're heavily into Spielberg,

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:28.090
naming E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, Close Encounters
of the Third Kind, and Jaws as big influences.

